WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:05.600
If you and I were to take every single millionaire,
billionaire, wealthy people that we know and

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.910
put them in one room, now obviously this would
be a good-sized room there - you would generally

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:15.469
be able to put all of these successful people
in three core competencies.

00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:21.520
You would say, this dude's strength is here,
this girl's strength is here, this partnership's

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.910
strength is here.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:24.070
That's how they made their wealth.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:27.900
So let me explain to you what those three
core competencies are.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:33.520
#1 is somebody who is extremely technically
sound.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.339
Let me explain to you what I mean by somebody
that's extremely technically sound.

00:00:36.339 --> 00:00:42.269
They know coding, they know laws, they know
laws about real estate, they know laws about,

00:00:42.269 --> 00:00:46.110
you know, investments, they know stocks, they
know charts, they know how to read charts.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.809
They know how to read trends.

00:00:47.809 --> 00:00:50.869
They know how to look at something there and
they figure out certain things that you may

00:00:50.869 --> 00:00:54.640
not even be paying attention to because you're
not the guy that's extremely technically sound.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.590
They can look at a certain, you know, projection
on an investment on a company and they'll

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:03.280
say, [snap] no, [snap] yes, what's going on,
this is a value-based company.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.280
Let's buy it.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.280
Let's build it.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.280
Let's re-engineer it.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.280
Let's bring a new executive team.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:11.340
Their brain is wired in a completely different
way because they're technically sound.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:16.040
#2 - The second type of competency that we're
talking about is leadership.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.070
Now, what is leadership?

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:20.220
Sometimes the guy that's very technical is
horrible about the leadership side.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:23.300
And sometimes the guy that does good at leadership
may be horrible on the technical side.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.280
Leadership is somebody who looks from the
outside and says, you know what, we need to

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.781
bring that person here and bring this person
here, and this department needs to be here,

00:01:29.781 --> 00:01:31.450
and this person's going to be driving this
part here.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.290
We need this department on this side here.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.190
I'm going to be able to bring that guy here.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.500
Let me try to recruit this other talent to
come here.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.940
Because they know how to lead an army.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:39.940
They know how to lead a team.

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:41.500
They know how to put a strong team together.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.350
And the last one, the third one I'm going
to tell you about on the core competencies

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:48.140
is not technical, it's not leadership.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.210
It's strategic.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:52.910
Strategic competency is people who know how
to put deals together.

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:59.659
They look at it and say, "I want to take 25%
of this here on this real estate deal and

00:01:59.659 --> 00:02:04.541
let's bring this person in with the money,
and let's create this partnership here, and

00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:09.810
if we sell it by this time, we'll be able
to sell it at . . . they're all strategy.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.620
It's slightly different than leadership.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:15.060
Strategic is slightly different than leadership
because leadership is more people.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.070
You're very good with people.

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:17.620
You're very good at driving people.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:23.459
Strategy has to do with timing, partnerships,
you know, teaming up with somebody, the enemy,

00:02:23.459 --> 00:02:26.730
the competition, when we take them out, when
we announce the comp, when we announce the

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.600
launch when we announce the initiative.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:29.740
That's strategy.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:30.800
Very, very different.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:36.280
And by the way, if you can find yourself in
a situation on a team where there's the technical,

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:42.870
there's a leader, and there's the strategic,
you put that together, now you're talking

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.710
about a powerhouse team that can be built.

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:47.010
But my message to you is very simple.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:49.319
Here's what my message to you is.

00:02:49.319 --> 00:02:51.900
You're not going to be able to do all three
of them.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:52.910
No one's going to be all three.

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:56.070
Now you may say, we'll this person was good
at all three of them, that person.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.510
. . Everybody typically has one core that
they're good at.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:02.180
And by the way, just because you may be watching
this saying oh, I'm very good at strategy,

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.319
I'm very good at leadership, I'm very good
at technical with coding, that still doesn't

00:03:05.319 --> 00:03:06.319
mean you're going to be a millionaire.

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.660
Because I don't know your work ethic.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:08.840
I don't know your fire.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:09.840
I don't know your desire.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:13.750
I don't know your willingness to get up and
get to work and go for years and, you know,

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.610
handling pressure and all that other stuff.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.290
I'm assuming you're willing to do that.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:18.930
I'm assuming you're willing to do that.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:22.320
If you're willing to do that, these are three
core competencies.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.129
One of them's got to be yours, technical,
leadership, or strategic.

00:03:26.129 --> 00:03:29.620
And then from there, you'll have a shot at
one day being a millionaire entrepreneur,

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.620
yourself as well.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:33.280
Now if you've got any questions, comments,
thoughts, be sure to comment on the bottom.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:40.879
And if you haven't subscribed to this channel,
be sure to subscribe to Valuetainment as well.

00:03:40.879 --> 00:03:44.319
Take care, everybody.

00:03:44.319 --> 00:03:46.620
Bye, bye.

